(42298,0,0,'With the power within the amulets of Razelikh...',12,0,100,0,0,0,''),
(42298,1,0,'... I bind you to his lair!',12,0,100,0,0,0,''),
(42308,3,0,'That\'s good to hear, marshal. While $n has brought the perpetrators to justice, their ringleader is still on the loose. Perhaps with the aid of the Westfall Brigade we will finally be able to solve this case.',12,0,100,1,0,0,'Lieutenant Horatio Laine to Player'),
(42308,4,0,'Might I ask, what\'s with the worgen in the stocks?',12,0,100,6,0,0,'Lieutenant Horatio Laine to Player'),
(42308,5,0,'Wow, the marshal wasn\'t kidding.',12,0,100,0,0,0,'Lieutenant Horatio Laine to Player'),
(42308,6,0,'But is your bark...',12,0,100,0,0,0,'Lieutenant Horatio Laine to Player'),
(42308,7,0,'Worse than your bite?',12,0,100,0,0,0,'Lieutenant Horatio Laine to Player'),
(42671,0,0,'This baby is all mine! I call her, "The Throttler."',12,0,100,66,0,0,'Chief Engineer to Player'),
(42671,0,1,'This baby is all mine! I call her, "The Throttler."',12,0,100,0,0,0,''),
(42671,0,2,'Ready for inspection! ...Be gentle.',12,0,100,0,0,0,''),
(42671,1,0,'Ready for inspection! ...Be gentle.',12,0,100,66,0,0,'Chief Engineer to Player'),
(42671,2,0,'Uh oh. Um. Oops.',12,0,100,0,0,0,'Chief Engineer to Player'),
(42671,3,0,'Look, look, it\'s okay! It\'s just a tiny little glitch. See?',12,0,100,0,0,0,'Chief Engineer to Player'),
(42744,0,0,'Just tell me one thing, Vanessa.',12,0,100,0,0,0,''),
(42744,1,0,'Why\'d you have the Furlbrows killed?',12,0,100,0,0,0,''),
(42748,0,0,'Thank you, my dear.',12,0,100,1,0,0,''),
(42749,0,0,'You bastards will burn for what you did.',12,0,100,25,0,0,''),
(42749,1,0,'Hope?  Like the hope Fandral had for bringing our people  back to glory?  Back to immortality?',12,0,100,1,0,0,''),
(42749,2,0,'Hope is a cruel joke, played upon us by a harsh and uncaring world. There is no Hope, there is only Vanessa. Vanessa VanCleef.',12,0,100,1,0,0,''),
(42749,3,0,'RISE UP BROTHERHOOD! THE DAWNING DAY IS UPON US!',14,0,100,22,0,0,''),
(42749,4,0,'Tie them up.',12,0,100,25,0,0,''),
(42749,5,0,'Admiral, your hat.',12,0,100,1,0,0,''),
(42749,6,0,'And you, $n, I will spare your life. You have done much to help our cause, albeit unwittingly, but the next time we meet it will be as enemies.',12,0,100,25,0,0,''),
(42749,7,0,'I had no choice, lieutenant. They recognized me. The only people in the world who even knew I existed, recognized my face from when I was an infant.',12,0,100,1,0,0,''),
(42749,8,0,'I took no pleasure in their deaths.',12,0,100,1,0,0,''),
(42749,9,0,'Leave nothing but ashes in your wake, brothers! Burn Sentinel Hill to the ground!',14,0,100,22,0,0,''),
(42750,0,0,'I don\'t like this, $n. Stay alert!',12,0,100,1,0,0,''),
(42750,1,0,'Hope! Wha..',12,0,100,5,0,0,''),
(42750,2,0,'$n, get to Stormwind. Tell King Wrynn everything. EVERYTHING! GO NOW!',12,0,100,0,0,0,''),
(42849,0,0,'Mekgineer Thermaplugg refuses to acknowledge that his defeat is imminent! He has sent Razlo Crushcog to prevent us from rebuilding our beloved Gnomeregan!',12,0,100,5,0,20890,'High Tinker Mekkatorque'),
(42849,1,0,'But $n has thwarted his plans at every turn, and the dwarves of Ironforge stand with us!',12,0,100,25,0,20891,'High Tinker Mekkatorque'),
(42849,2,0,'Let\'s send him crawling back to his master in defeat!',12,0,100,5,0,20892,'High Tinker Mekkatorque'),
(42849,3,0,'We\'ve done it! We\'re victorious!',12,0,100,5,0,20893,'High Tinker Mekkatorque'),
(42849,4,0,'With Crushcog defeated, Thermaplugg is sure to be quaking in his mechano-tank, and rightly so. You\'re next Thermaplugg. You\'re next!',12,0,100,5,0,20894,'High Tinker Mekkatorque'),
(42849,5,0,'Mekkatorque-Cannon!',14,0,100,0,0,0,'High Tinker Mekkatorque'),
(42849,6,0,'Mekkatorque-Ray!',14,0,100,0,0,0,'High Tinker Mekkatorque'),
(42849,7,0,'Mekkatorque-Missiles!',14,0,100,0,0,0,'High Tinker Mekkatorque'),
(42849,8,0,'Mekkatorque-Beam!',14,0,100,0,0,0,'High Tinker Mekkatorque'),
(42852,0,0,'Aye, let\'s teach this addle-brained gnome a lesson!',12,0,100,25,0,0,'Mountaineer Stonegrind'),
(42852,1,0,'That\'ll teach you to mess with the might of Ironforge and Gnomeregan!',12,0,100,25,0,0,'Mountaineer Stonegrind'),
